  "name": "Automate a 'Chat with your PDF' Bot on Telegram with Google Gemini & Pinecone",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "e2b02a33-dd65-43a2-9d8c-b2d4a46418ef",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -32,
        528
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Development Done - Chat with PDF via Telegram\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow lets users chat with PDFs through Telegram. Incoming Telegram messages are routed based on whether they contain a document: PDF files are downloaded, normalized, split, embedded, and stored in Pinecone, while text questions are answered by a Gemini-powered retrieval QA chain using the stored document context. The workflow sends Telegram confirmations after indexing and Telegram answers after question processing, then stops execution cleanly.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure Telegram credentials for both the Telegram Trigger and Telegram send/get-file nodes, and connect them to the intended bot.\n- Configure Google Gemini credentials for the chat model and embedding nodes.\n- Create or select the Pinecone index used by both vector store nodes, and ensure its dimension/metric matches the Gemini embedding model.\n- Verify the document branch maps the Telegram file ID and binary data correctly, and that the code node sets the uploaded file metadata to application/pdf.\n- Set the Telegram response nodes to send messages back to the correct chat ID from the incoming update.\n\n### Customization\n\nYou can adjust the text splitter chunk size/overlap, change the Gemini model, swap the vector database, or modify the Telegram response messages for indexing confirmations and QA answers."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "9c2861fb-e420-41d8-b08a-4d480d5dbb81",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        528,
        1120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Telegram intake routing\n\nReceives incoming Telegram updates and checks whether the message is a document or a regular question, sending the workflow down the upload or QA path."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b0ef3109-f7f6-412f-925c-4d631a1acce1",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1360,
        848
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 512,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Download and prepare PDF\n\nFetches the uploaded Telegram file and adjusts the binary metadata so the downstream document loader treats it as a PDF."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "7e8dceb5-3ddb-4110-9720-13849034b0da",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2064,
        528
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 384,
        "height": 672,
        "content": "## Embed and index document\n\nLoads the prepared PDF, splits it into chunks, creates Gemini embeddings, and stores the resulting vectors in Pinecone for later retrieval."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "fe7a8b49-6462-44dd-b1b6-736f99a99902",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2512,
        576
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 736,
        "height": 400,
        "content": "## Confirm database update\n\nLimits the indexing output to a single item, sends a Telegram confirmation about the database update, and stops that branch."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c5070570-d831-461b-a679-67a76cebadae",
      "name": "Sticky Note5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1488,
        1264
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 480,
        "height": 848,
        "content": "## Answer with retrieval\n\nUses a retrieval QA chain backed by Pinecone and Gemini embeddings to find relevant document chunks, then has the Gemini chat model generate an answer."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
